-- title:
--   Row-10 square-coefficient block 0 and reduced multiplier product
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-10 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/20-66\alpha+21\alpha^2$. Let $s_j(\alpha)$ be the coefficients of the reduced square polynomial $S_\alpha$. This file defines the block
--   $$S_{\alpha,0}(t)=\sum_{j=0}^{15}s_{j+0}(\alpha)t^j$$
--   and the explicit reduced product polynomial $U_{\alpha,0}(t)$. Its coefficients are rational quadratic expressions in $\alpha$. The identity $Q_\alpha(t)S_{\alpha,0}(t)=U_{\alpha,0}(t)$ is proved separately. The four adjacent blocks together cover all 63 coefficients of $S_\alpha$ and let the inverse residual be verified in bounded arithmetic stages.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

